course: dictionary
lesson: 2884
title: Doorway: a place, not just a door
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A doorway is the opening in a wall where a door is. It can also mean the space just inside or just outside a door. When you meet this word, check the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: «The first time Jake did it, he stood in the office doorway with his fists still clenched.» The words stood and office tell you Jake was in the opening of the office door, not in the middle of the room. Swap in your meaning: "he stood in the opening where the office door is" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: Doorway is also used in phrases such as «stand in the doorway» and «block the doorway». To block a doorway is to stop people getting through the opening. Look at the verb next to the word, and it often tells you what the doorway is being used for.
fact: A doorway is the opening in a wall where a door is.
fact: A doorway can also mean the space just inside or outside a door.
fact: «Stand in the doorway» means to stand in the opening, and «block the doorway» means to stop people getting through.
fact: In a story, a figure who appears in the doorway often shows that someone has arrived.
fact: January is named after Janus, the Roman god of doorways, who had two faces.
exercise: «The first time Jake did it, he stood in the office doorway with his fists still clenched.» Where did Jake stand? | On the playground | *In the office doorway | In the head teacher's car | Under the table
exercise: What is a doorway? | A type of window with a curtain | *The opening in a wall where a door is | The roof above the front step | A staircase inside a house
exercise: Which phrase means stopping people from getting through the opening? | stand in the doorway | *block the doorway | paint the doorway blue | welcome the doorway
test: «Lily stayed on the line from her doorway until the ambulance came.» Where was Lily while she was on the phone? | *Inside or just outside her house, at the opening of the door | On a bus to town | Fighting with the older boys | On the ambulance
test: In a story, a figure appears in the doorway. What does this most likely show? | Someone is leaving forever | *Someone has arrived | The door is broken | The house is empty
exam: The space just inside or just outside a door is called what? | The floor | The roof | *The doorway | The stairs
